 * visa" exists. Content status is 'researched' throughout, for the same
 * WebFetch-blocked-sandbox reason documented in prior batches.
 *
 * Outcomes genuinely vary: a distinct sponsor-based Family Visit Visa
 * exists in the Gulf states (UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman,
 * Bahrain), Ireland (Short Stay 'C' — Visit Family or Friend), Indonesia
 * (a Visit Visa subtype) and South Korea (F-1); Thailand's Non-Immigrant
 * "O" (Family) applies only when the host is a Thai *national*, not just
 * a Thai resident; South Africa's Visitor's Visa explicitly names
 * family/friends as a stated purpose with its own host-undertaking
 * document; Japan uses its ordinary Temporary Visitor visa with a
 * relative-specific documentation track (distinct from the long-term
 * Dependent visa, which does not apply to a short visit); and for the
 * remaining countries (the Schengen six, Singapore, Malaysia, Vietnam,
 * Sri Lanka, Maldives, Mauritius, Kenya, Turkey, Egypt) there is honestly
 * no standalone family-visit category — family visits are documented as
 * using the country's standard tourist/visitor visa instead. Nepal remains
 * not applicable, consistent with its Tourist/Transit Visa records.
 *
 * Loaded from visa_content_db() alongside the other seed files; each entry
 * upgrades the matching bulk-generic page in place via visa_seed_page() /
 * visa_seed_page_upgrade() — it never overwrites a page that has already
 * moved past 'generic' status.
 */
